// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/test-a-page.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeTestAPage(path: "/recipes/test-a-page", title: "Test a page — Recipes", description: "Write tests under tests/ that render a component or a page, type and click through it like a reader, and check what it shows; run them with wf test.") {
    RecipeShell("Test a page", summary: "A test renders a component or a whole page, acts on it the way a reader does — typing, clicking, pressing keys — and checks the text the page shows. This shopping list has a component that counts, a page that adds items, and three tests:", outputs: ["website", "app", "desktop"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "variations", label: "Variations")], related: [], source: "md-docs/recipes/test-a-page.md", how: true, hasVariations: true) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** a `tests/` folder beside `src/`, and a Chrome or Chromium on the machine for the tests that click (or `WF_CHROME` naming one). The block holds three files; the comment above each says where it goes.")
            CodeBlock(#"// src/components/Count.wf
component Count(_ n: Number) {
    Text(if n == 1 { "1 thing to buy" } else { "{n} things to buy" })
}

// src/pages/Shopping.wf
page Shopping(path: "/shopping", title: "Shopping", description: "What to buy.") {
    state items: [String] = ["Milk"]
    state draft = ""

    Heading("Shopping").h1
    Count(items.length)
    Form {
        on submit(e) {
            e.preventDefault()
            if draft != "" { items = items.concat([draft]) }
            draft = ""
        }
        Input(bind: draft, label: "Item")
        Button("Add", type: .submit).primary
    }
    for item in items by item { Text(item) }
}

// tests/shopping.wf
test "one thing reads in the singular" {
    Count(1)
    expect "1 thing to buy"
    expect not "things"
}

test "adding an item lists it and counts it" {
    Shopping
    expect "1 thing to buy"
    type "Bread" into "Item"
    click "Add"
    expect "Bread"
    expect "2 things to buy"
}

test "an empty item is not added" {
    Shopping
    click "Add"
    expect "1 thing to buy"
}"#, title: "wf")
            Markdown("Run them:")
            Terminal(lines: [
                        Line(command: "wf test")
                    ])
            CodeBlock(#"  new   tests/shopping.wf — one thing reads in the singular (snapshot written)
  ok    tests/shopping.wf — adding an item lists it and counts it (in a browser)
  ok    tests/shopping.wf — an empty item is not added (in a browser)
3 passed, 0 failed, 1 snapshot(s) written"#, title: "text")
        }
        variations {
            Markdown("- **Seed the state**: `test \"…\"(data: \{ items: [\"a\", \"b\"] \}) \{ … \}` starts the body's state, or a store by its name, with that data.\n- **Close a dialog**: `press \"Escape\"` closes the open `Modal` or `Dialog`; `press \"Enter\" in \"Search\"` presses a key in one named field.\n- **One file**: `wf test tests/shopping.wf` runs only that file's tests.\n- **Every page in a browser**: `wf verify` loads each route of the built site and fails on a script error, a failed request or a page that drew nothing ([Testing](/learn/16-testing#check-every-page-with-wf-verify)).\n- **In CI**: run `wf check`, `wf test` and `wf build` in that order ([Install wf on a build machine](/recipes/install-wf-in-ci)).\n\nA key step names one key, as the browser names it (`\"Enter\"`, `\"Escape\"`, `\"a\"`); it does not hold a modifier, so a shortcut such as Ctrl+K is checked by calling what it runs.")

        }
        Markdown("- `wf test` runs every `test \"…\" \{ \}` under `tests/`. A build ignores them, so they never reach the site.\n- A test's body is drawn like a page's: `Count(1)` places the component, and `Shopping`, a page with no route parameter, is placed by its name. The project's components, stores, types and constants are all in reach.\n- `expect \"…\"` checks the text a reader would see, with white space collapsed the way a browser lays it out, never the markup. `expect not \"…\"` checks that it is absent.\n- A test with a step that acts — `click`, `type … into`, `press` — is built into a real page and run in headless Chrome, so the handler runs, the state changes and the page draws again. `type \"Bread\" into \"Item\"` finds the field by its label, and `click \"Add\"` the button by its text: by what a reader sees, so a test also catches a control that lost its name.\n- A test that only looks needs no browser. It is rendered and compared with a snapshot, `tests/__snapshots__/shopping/<test name>.html`, written the first time it runs. When a change is meant, `wf test --update` writes the snapshots again; commit them with the code.\n- A handler that throws fails the test, so a broken click is caught even when the text happens to match.")

    }
}
